    "title": "EXCLUSIVE VIDEO: Dot-Marie Jones On Becoming LGBTQ Icon Playing Transgender Man On 'Glee' - NewsBreak",
    "text": "In conversation with uInterview, Dot-Marie Jones , who played Coach Beiste, a transgender man, in the series, recalled the heartwarming experience of being thanked by trans individuals for her portrayal of the character. “They said, ‘I never thought I’d see myself on TV.’” Airing from 2009 to 2015, Glee was a pioneer in LGBTQ representation. Featuring multiple openly queer characters and storylines that encouraged acceptance of all sexual identities, Glee normalized LGBTQ representation in the media.",
